### User Story 4 - Comments Creation Acceptance Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost/api
### Prerequisites: 
### - Run this after Phase 5 (US3) is complete
### - Requires existing posts and authenticated users from seed data or previous tests
### - Get access token from login endpoint first

### 1. Create comment on existing post (success)
# @name createComment
POST http://localhost/api/posts/{{postId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "content": "This is a test comment on the post"
}

### Expected: 201 Created with comment details including commentId, postId, author, content, createdAt

###

### 2. Create comment without authentication (401)
POST http://localhost/api/posts/{{postId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This should fail without auth"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - Authentication required

###

### 3. Create comment with empty content (400)
POST http://localhost/api/posts/{{postId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "content": ""
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Content is required

###

### 4. Create comment with only whitespace (400)
POST http://localhost/api/posts/{{postId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "content": "   "
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Content cannot be empty

###

### 5. Create comment on non-existent post (404)
POST http://localhost/api/posts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "content": "Comment on non-existent post"
}

### Expected: 404 Not Found - Post not found

###

### 5b. Create comment with invalid postId format (400)
POST http://localhost/api/posts/invalid-uuid/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "content": "Comment on invalid post ID"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Invalid post ID format

###

### 6. Create comment on soft-deleted post (404)
# First, create and delete a post (requires author access token)
# @name createTestPost
POST http://localhost/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authorAccessToken}}

{
  "content": "This post will be deleted for testing"
}

###

# @name deleteTestPost
DELETE http://localhost/api/posts/{{createTestPost.response.body.postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authorAccessToken}}

###

# Now try to comment on the deleted post (should fail)
POST http://localhost/api/posts/{{createTestPost.response.body.postId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "content": "Comment on deleted post"
}

### Expected: 404 Not Found - Post not found

###

### 7. Get comments list includes newly created comment (verify)
GET http://localhost/api/posts/{{postId}}/comments?limit=20&offset=0

### Expected: 200 OK with list containing the comment created in test #1

###

### 8. Get comments on soft-deleted post (404)
GET http://localhost/api/posts/{{createTestPost.response.body.postId}}/comments

### Expected: 404 Not Found - Post not found

###

### Setup Instructions:
### 1. Replace {{postId}} with an actual post ID from seed data or create a new post
### 2. Replace {{accessToken}} with a valid JWT token from login
### 3. Replace {{authorAccessToken}} with a token for a user who can create/delete posts
### 4. Run tests sequentially to ensure proper setup

### Example setup:
# Login first
# @name login
POST http://localhost/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345678",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Use the accessToken from login response in subsequent requests
